{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Do not hasten to depart.</b> We find in this language: ונדעה נרדפה (1 Samuel 17:55), אל תרבו תדברו (Ecclesiastes 5:1). Their essence: ונדע לרדוף, אל תרבו לדבר. And more correct is that the שי״ן is missing, which stands in place of אשר, and it would be thus: ונדעה שנרדפה, אל תרבו שתדברו. And likewise this word תלך: אל תבהל מפניו ללכת — or אל תבהל מפניו: let your heart not be hasty to think that you can depart from before the king's face, lest you stand upon a matter that is evil in his eyes, for as his will he can do to you."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:21.010740490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}